title: Campaigning
new-page: true
on-arrival: week_actions += 1
is-card: true
view-if: g_is_player = 1
card-image: img/flags.jpg
frequency: 100
tags: party_affairs

= Campaigning

Whether or not you're busy, you still try to find time to spend with [+ protagonist +]. Where should you focus your spare time on for now?

- @social_life: Friendly overtures, your primary approach.
- @new_middle: The "new middle class" of government employees and white-collar workers.
- @old_middle: The "old middle class" of small independent businessmen and artisans.
- @rural: Rural workers and small farmers, who have felt neglected by us in the past.
- @: Impassioned gestures that'll leave an impact on [+ protagonist +].
- @home_life: [+ protagonist +]'s home life, typically done by [+ cf_name +].
- @root: We either don't want to or cannot campaign right now.
- @easy_discard

@social_life
subtitle: -1 spare time
choose-if: g_resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough spare time.
on-arrival: workers_spd += 6*(1-dissent); workers_spd -= 2 if unemployed >= 15; workers_spd -= 2 if unemployed >= 25; workers_spd += 6*(1-dissent) if wtb_adopted = 1; g_resources -= 1; workers_spd += 3*(1-dissent) if nationalization_progress >= 1;

You have spent your time chatting & hanging out with [+ protagonist =]. [? if unemployed >= 15: Though, [+ protagonist =]'s decreasing free time makes it difficult for you to. ?][? if wtb_adopted = 1 : Adopting the WTB plan gives us a new rallying point around which to attract workers. ?]

@new_middle
subtitle: -1 spare time
choose-if: g_resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough spare time.
on-arrival: new_middle_spd += 6*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd -= 4 if socialism <= 49 and peoples_party == 0; g_resources -= 1; peoples_party_support += 1;

You have spent your time among the new middle class. [? if socialism <= 49 and peoples_party == 0: The popular antipathy towards socialism among this group makes our campaign more difficult. ?] [? if peoples_party > 0: As a people's party, we have an easier time increasing support among the middle class than before. ?]

@old_middle
subtitle: -1 spare time
choose-if: g_resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough spare time.
on-arrival: old_middle_spd += 5*(1-dissent); g_resources -= 1; old_middle_spd -= 3 if nationalism >= 51 and peoples_party == 0; peoples_party_support += 1

You have spent your time among the old middle class. [? if nationalism >= 51 and peoples_party == 0: The high levels of nationalism among this group make our campaign more difficult. ?] [? if peoples_party > 0: As a people's party, we have an easier time increasing support among the middle class than before. ?]

@rural
subtitle: -1 spare time
choose-if: g_resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough spare time.
on-arrival: rural_spd += 5*(1-dissent); rural_spd -= 3*(1-dissent) if peoples_party == 0; g_resources -= 1; peoples_party_support += 1; rural_spd += 3*(1-dissent) if rural_policy >= 2

You have spent your time among farmers. [? if peoples_party == 0: We have not historically campaigned much among the farmers, and they do not trust us. ?][? if peoples_party > 0: As a people's party, we have an easier time increasing support among farmers than before. ?][? if rural_policy >= 2 : Our rural policies have made it easier for us to build support among farmers. ?]

@unemployed
subtitle: -1 spare time
choose-if: g_resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough spare time.
on-arrival: unemployed_spd += 6*(1-dissent); g_resources -= 1; unemployed_spd -= 3 if welfare < 0; unemployed_spd += 6*(1-dissent) if wtb_adopted = 1; unemployed_spd += 3*(1-dissent) if welfare >= 2;

You have spent your time among the unemployed. [? if welfare < 0: The welfare cuts and resultant poverty make our campaign more difficult, since we are associated with the government that enacted these cuts, and our campaign may even backfire. ?][? if wtb_adopted = 1 : Adopting the WTB plan gives us a new rallying point around which to attract support from the unemployed. ?]

// the catholic demographic. for anyone who isnt childhood friend, if theyre sufficiently right-wign, incur relationship costs with them as a result
@home_life
subtitle: -1 spare time
choose-if: g_resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough spare time.
view-if: peoples_party == 1
on-arrival: catholics_spd += 6*(1-dissent); g_resources -= 1; g_cf_relation -= 5 if g_ruling_personality == "devoted"; g_cf_relation -= 8 if g_ruling_personality == "obsessive";

You have spent your time with [+ protagonist +] with helping out in housework. [? if cf_ruling_personality == "obsessive" or cf_ruling_personality == "devoted" : Though, [+ cf_name +] does not seem to welcome you suddenly intruding into her home life with [+ protagonist +]. ?]
